.TH GIT-RELEASE 1 "2026-02-21" "ShellScript Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-release \- automated semantic versioning releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-release
[\fIpatch|minor|major\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Automates semantic version bumping and GitHub releases.

Determines current version from git tags, bumps according to
SemVer rules, creates annotated tag, and pushes to GitHub.

Triggers GitHub's auto-generated release notes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR patch (default)
Increment patch version: 1.0.0 → 1.0.1
.TP
.B minor
Increment minor version: 1.0.0 → 1.1.0
.TP
.B major
Increment major version: 1.0.0 → 2.0.0
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git-release patch
Release 1.0.1 from 1.0.0
.TP
.B git-release minor
Release 1.1.0 — new features, backward compatible
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Clean git working directory.
All changes committed before release.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-tag (1),
.BR git-push (1),
.BR semantic-versioning (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Fabbio for ShellScript Toolkit Pro
